From 3afad617626397431bcf9a78b48fff029780720a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 04:52:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(rlsm): restore word-box scale parameter lost in the
 main merge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

317edd1 (Merge branch 'main') reverted fr24/rlsm_wordboxes.py to the version
without the `scale` parameter and took both call sites with it. main never
carried this file — PR 121 is not merged — so this was not a content conflict,
just a resolution that took the wrong side.

tests/test_rlsm_ocr_preprocessing.py caught it: 4 failed, 55 passed, all four
on TypeError: unexpected keyword argument 'scale'.

The failure the tests exist to prevent is the quiet one. Preprocessing upscales
each crop 2x before Tesseract sees it, so word boxes come back in scaled
coordinates. Without the division every stored pin coordinate is doubled, the
affine geocoder fits those points without complaint, and the error only
surfaces as wrong lat/lon much further downstream.

Restores fr24/rlsm_wordboxes.py, fr24/rlsm_ocr_parallel.py and fr24/rlsm_ocr.py
to their state at 71e9ceb. 59 passed.

